{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3277","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3277","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3277\",\"parent_revision\":\"dbe92fe39f38b503d5553f409269e00c2f06f606\",\"root_revision\":\"471a908220f47c47eafb3b3414becf252e873a9894fadffdfdb760df024fbadc\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-28\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nObserved 2026-08-28/29 while running `/dh:work-backlog-item work --auto #3268`: `dh:swarm-task-planner` produced plan Pb31107bf with a populated `acceptance-criteria-structured` list (6 entries, each with a `check-command`, `expected-baseline`, and `expected-final`), but generated no `T0` or `TN` bookend tasks.\\n\\n`implement-feature/SKILL.md`'s \\\"Bookend Task Ordering\\\" section states this is not optional: \\\"When the plan contains `acceptance-criteria-structured` entries, `swarm-task-planner` generates T0 and TN bookend tasks. No special handling is needed in this loop \u2014 existing readiness logic dispatches them in the correct order automatically.\\\" T0 (`t0-baseline-capture`, `priority: 1`, `dependencies: []`) is meant to be the first ready task, capturing real command output before any implementation edit lands. TN (`tn-verification-gate`, `dependencies: [all non-bookend task IDs]`) is meant to run last, re-running the same commands and registering a `TN-verification` artifact for `/dh:complete-implementation`'s Pre-Phase-1 check.\\n\\nPlan Pb31107bf's task list is T1, T2, T3, T4, T5, T6 only \u2014 no T0, no TN \u2014 despite carrying a fully-formed `acceptance-criteria-structured` array that is exactly the input the Bookend Task Ordering contract says triggers their generation.\\n\\n**Consequence, verified by reading `complete-implementation/SKILL.md`'s Pre-Phase 1 TN Verification Check**: when the `TN-verification` artifact is absent, the check treats it as \\\"No structured criteria \u2014 proceed to Phase 1\\\" and silently skips verification entirely. This is indistinguishable, from the gate's perspective, from a plan that genuinely has no structured acceptance criteria to verify \u2014 it does not distinguish \\\"nothing to check\\\" from \\\"something to check that was never captured.\\\" The plan's 6 structured criteria therefore never get an independent, empirically-measured before/after comparison: each implementation task's own verification-steps duplicate the equivalent grep check, but those are self-reported by the same agent that made the edit, not an independent T0 baseline measured before any edit landed, and no single TN pass re-runs all 6 checks together after everything completes to catch cross-task regressions.\\n\\nUser-provided context: none \u2014 the fix (why `swarm-task-planner` skipped bookend generation for this input) has not been investigated; this item captures the observed defect and its verified downstream consequence, not a diagnosed root cause.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T15:08:29.705868Z</sub>\\n\\n```\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: Plan Pb31107bf has a populated acceptance-criteria-structured list with 6 entries, each carrying check-command, expected-baseline, and expected-final.\\nevidence: mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_plan(config={\\\"action\\\": \\\"read\\\"}, plan=\\\"Pb31107bf\\\") returned plan object with acceptance-criteria-structured array containing AC1-AC6, each with fields: criterion-id, description, check-command, expected-baseline, expected-final.\\nsource: Plan Pb31107bf, acceptance-criteria-structured list (6 entries indexed AC1 through AC6)\\n```\\n\\n```\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: Plan Pb31107bf's task list is exactly T1, T2, T3, T4, T5, T6 \u2014 no T0 task with bookend-type: t0-baseline, no TN/T99 task with bookend-type: tn-verification.\\nevidence: mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_plan(config={\\\"action\\\": \\\"read\\\"}, plan=\\\"Pb31107bf\\\") returned plan with tasks array containing exactly six task objects with id values T1, T3, T4, T5, T2, T6. All tasks have bookend-type: null (not set). No task carries bookend-type: t0-baseline or bookend-type: tn-verification.\\nsource: Plan Pb31107bf, tasks array (6 entries)\\n```\\n\\n```\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md's \\\"Bookend Task Ordering\\\" section states (words to this effect): \\\"When the plan contains acceptance-criteria-structured entries, swarm-task-planner generates T0 and TN bookend tasks... No special handling is needed in this loop.\\\"\\nevidence: File implement-feature/SKILL.md line 311-314 contains exact wording: \\\"When the plan contains `acceptance-criteria-structured` entries, `swarm-task-planner` generates T0 and TN bookend tasks. No special handling is needed in this loop \u2014 existing readiness logic dispatches them in the correct order automatically\\\"\\nsource: /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md:311-314\\n```\\n\\n```\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md already contains explicit, mandatory-sounding instructions for bookend generation (a \\\"Bookend Task Generation\\\" section around line 328, and a \\\"Bookend presence check\\\" self-verification step around line 605) \u2014 the omission in Pb31107bf was not caused by the agent's instructions being silent or ambiguous.\\nevidence: File swarm-task-planner.md line 328 contains section \\\"## Bookend Task Generation\\\" with line 330 stating \\\"When the plan's `acceptance-criteria-structured` field is non-empty, automatically generate two bookend tasks: T0 (baseline capture) and TN (verification gate).\\\" Line 605 contains \\\"12. Bookend presence check (when `acceptance-criteria-structured` is non-empty)\\\" with detailed mandatory checks for T0 and TN task properties.\\nsource: /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md:328-349 (Bookend Task Generation section) and 605-612 (Bookend presence check step)\\n```\\n\\n```\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md's Pre-Phase-1 \\\"TN Verification Check\\\" treats an absent TN-verification artifact the same as \\\"no structured criteria to verify\\\" and proceeds to Phase 1 without flagging the discrepancy.\\nevidence: File complete-implementation/SKILL.md line 317-318 shows mermaid diagram branch: \\\"Exists -->|No| Proceed[\\\"No structured criteria \u2014 proceed to Phase 1\\\"]\\\" and line 306 states \\\"When it is absent, proceed to Phase 1 because no artifact owner is addressable.\\\" The section explicitly treats missing TN-verification artifact as equivalent condition to \\\"no structured criteria\\\" with no error or discrepancy flag.\\nsource: /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md:300-324 (Pre-Phase 1 TN Verification Check section including flowchart)\\n```\\n\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T15:03:45.811693Z</sub>\\n\\n<details><summary>struck: 2026-08-28T15:23:41.685828Z \u2014 Final RT-ICA pass after Wave 1 swarm findings (impact-analyst, fact-checker, classifier)</summary>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: fix: swarm-task-planner does not generate T0/TN bookend tasks for plans with acceptance-criteria-structured\\nDate: 2026-08-29\\nGoal: Determine why swarm-task-planner produced plan Pb31107bf with a populated acceptance-criteria-structured list but no T0/TN bookend tasks, and fix the root cause.\\nConditions:\\n1. Why did swarm-task-planner skip generating T0/TN despite non-empty acceptance-criteria-structured in plan Pb31107bf? | Status: MISSING\\n2. Does the swarm-task-planner agent's own instructions correctly specify bookend generation as mandatory for non-empty acceptance-criteria-structured? | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. Is this a one-time occurrence specific to plan Pb31107bf, or a systemic/reproducible failure across other plans carrying acceptance-criteria-structured? | Status: DERIVABLE\\n4. What is the actual current content of plan Pb31107bf (confirm acceptance-criteria-structured is genuinely non-empty, confirm task list is exactly T1-T6)? | Status: DERIVABLE\\n5. Does the defect lie in agent instruction-following (the agent skipped its own self-check step) or in a code/schema gap (e.g., sam-schema does not enforce bookend presence at plan-registration time)? | Status: MISSING\\nAVAILABLE count: 1\\nDERIVABLE count: 2\\nMISSING count: 2\\n</details>\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T15:23:41.685893Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final Assessment: fix: swarm-task-planner does not generate T0/TN bookend tasks for plans with acceptance-criteria-structured\\nDate: 2026-08-29\\nGoal: Determine why swarm-task-planner produced plan Pb31107bf with a populated acceptance-criteria-structured list but no T0/TN bookend tasks, and plan the root-cause fix.\\n\\n## Conditions\\n\\n| # | Condition | Wave 1 Finding | Status | Evidence |\\n|---|-----------|---|--------|----------|\\n| 1 | Why did swarm-task-planner skip generating T0/TN despite non-empty `acceptance-criteria-structured` in plan Pb31107bf? | Root-Cause Analysis: `BookendValidator` exists (dependencies.py:276-391) with complete logic and unit tests, but is **structurally isolated** from all plan-write operations (`create_plan`, `finalize_plan`, `append_task` in operations.py). Zero calls from any backend or MCP handler. This is a code/schema **gap**, not agent instruction-following failure. | AVAILABLE | Root-Cause Analysis claims 1-5 (VERIFIED); Impact-analyst scope expansion: `BookendValidator` never called from operations.py, server.py, or any backend. |\\n| 2 | Does swarm-task-planner's own instructions correctly specify bookend generation as mandatory for non-empty `acceptance-criteria-structured`? | Fact-Checker Claim 4 (VERIFIED): swarm-task-planner.md lines 328-349 \\\"Bookend Task Generation\\\" section + lines 605-612 \\\"Bookend presence check\\\" step both mandate T0/TN generation. Instructions are explicit and mandatory-sounding. | AVAILABLE | Fact-Check verified claim 4 with exact line numbers and quoted text. |\\n| 3 | Is this a one-time occurrence specific to plan Pb31107bf, or a systemic/reproducible failure affecting all plans carrying non-empty `acceptance-criteria-structured`? | Impact-Analyst Scope Expansion (9 systems): Identified that `BookendValidator` gap exists at the unified write-path layer (operations.py). All plan creation/finalization routes through this layer regardless of plan content, source (CLI/MCP), or backend (local/GitHub/beads). Gap is **systemic** \u2014 affects any plan with structured criteria, not just Pb31107bf. | AVAILABLE | Impact-Radius scope expansion: operations.py create/finalize/append have zero BookendValidator references; all backends delegate to this layer; grep-confirmed no validation wired anywhere. |\\n| 4 | What is the actual current content of plan Pb31107bf (verify `acceptance-criteria-structured` is non-empty, verify task list is exactly T1\u2013T6)? | Fact-Checker Claims 1\u20132 (both VERIFIED): Plan Pb31107bf carries 6 `acceptance-criteria-structured` entries (AC1\u2013AC6) and task list is exactly [T1, T3, T4, T5, T2, T6] \u2014 no T0, no TN. Verified via direct SAM MCP read. | AVAILABLE | Fact-Check verified claims 1\u20132 with evidence from `sam_plan` MCP read of plan Pb31107bf. |\\n| 5 | Does the defect lie in swarm-task-planner's instruction-following (agent skipped its own self-check) or in a code/schema gap (e.g., `BookendValidator` exists but is never called)? | Root-Cause Analysis (VERIFIED): Defect is **code/schema gap**. The validator exists fully-formed and correctly-implemented in isolation (dependencies.py, with full unit test coverage), but no runtime control flow instantiates or calls it. Agent's documented self-check cannot execute a validation that