eria scoped to enforcing BookendValidator at the schema layer and effort estimates calibrated to a known, bounded integration task.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T15:10:36.799230Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type**: defect\\n\\n**Rationale**: Traceable failure with identifiable cause chain. The agent had explicit documented instructions (swarm-task-planner.md \u00a7328-379) to generate T0/TN bookend tasks when `acceptance-criteria-structured` is non-empty, and a mandatory self-check gate (\u00a7605-612) requiring verification before plan registration. Plan Pb31107bf carries non-empty `acceptance-criteria-structured` (6 entries) but zero bookend tasks, indicating the self-check either was skipped or failed silently.\\n\\n**Analysis Method**: Direct observation + code inspection\\n\\n**Scenario Target**: Execution \u2192 Verification Gate Failure: The bookend-presence check at Phase 4 Step 12 should have blocked plan registration; the fact that it did not indicates either (1) the check logic itself is faulty, (2) the check was silently skipped, or (3) there is a code/schema gap making the check incomplete.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T15:09:25.047969Z</sub>\\n\\nSCOPE_EXPANSION: 9 systems beyond the 5 named in the grooming brief \u2014 a schema-level `BookendValidator` (dependencies.py) exists with full unit coverage but is never called from any plan-creation/finalize code path (CLI, MCP, or backend), which is the concrete schema/validation-gap finding this item's RT-ICA needs. Listed under Code-Producers/Code-Consumers below.\\n\\n## Systems Inventory\\n\\n| # | System | Role | Verified |\\n|---|--------|------|----------|\\n| 1 | `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` (Bookend Task Generation \u00a7328-391, self-check step 12 \u00a7605-612) | Producer \u2014 LLM-followed instructions to emit T0/TN | Confirmed, line numbers match brief |\\n| 2 | Plan `Pb31107bf` | Concrete artifact missing T0/TN despite 6 structured criteria | Not independently re-read here (MCP `sam_plan` read not exercised in this pass) \u2014 treat as MISSING/unverified, flag for rtica-assessor |\\n| 3 | `skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` (Bookend Task Ordering) | Consumer \u2014 dispatch-ordering contract assumes T0/TN exist | Confirmed present |\\n| 4 | `skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` (Pre-Phase 1 TN Verification Check, lines 300-324) | Consumer \u2014 silently proceeds when `TN-verification` artifact is absent | Confirmed; mermaid line 318 literally mislabels \\\"artifact absent\\\" as \\\"No structured criteria\\\" \u2014 conflates two different causes |\\n| 5 | `sam_schema/core/dependencies.py::BookendValidator` (lines ~276-391) | **New finding** \u2014 schema-level validator enforcing all 5 bookend structural rules, including \\\"structured criteria require both bookend tasks\\\" | Confirmed to exist and be fully correct in isolation |\\n| 6 | `sam_schema/__init__.py` | Exports `BookendValidator` publicly | Confirmed export, no internal caller |\\n| 7 | `dh_core/operations.py::create_plan`, `append_task`, `finalize_plan` | **New finding** \u2014 the only call sites that could invoke `BookendValidator`; none do | Confirmed via grep + read, no `Bookend` reference anywhere in operations.py |\\n| 8 | `sam_schema/server.py` (`_sam_plan_create`, `_sam_plan_finalize`, MCP `sam_plan` action dispatch) | **New finding** \u2014 MCP layer delegates straight to `operations.py`, no validation | Confirmed |\\n| 9 | `sam_schema/core/backends/{local_yaml,github_task,beads}.py::finalize_plan` | **New finding** \u2014 each backend's finalize is a bare state transition (drafting\u2192ready / no-op), no bookend check | Confirmed by reading all three implementations |\\n| 10 | `tests_sam/test_dependencies.py` (TestBookendValidator*) | Full unit coverage of the validator in isolation \u2014 passes in CI, gives false confidence since nothing calls the validator | Confirmed |\\n| 11 | `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml` (line 244, `uv run pytest`) | Runs the above unit tests; no integration/E2E test asserts a plan *cannot* finalize with structured criteria and no bookends | Confirmed \u2014 broad pytest invocation, no dedicated bookend-enforcement CI gate |\\n| 12 | `docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` (P4_BOOKEND flow, lines ~395-421, 533-536) | Documents the intended flow as if the swarm-task-planner's compliance were guaranteed; no mention of a runtime guard | Confirmed |\\n| 13 | `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` (lines 292-293, 388-389) | Documents `is-bookend`/`bookend-type` fields | Confirmed, accurate to schema |\\n| 14 | `README.md`, `AGENTS.md` | User-facing mentions of T0/TN bookend behavior | Confirmed, descriptive only, no contract detail to fix |\\n| 15 | `agents/t0-baseline-capture.md`, `agents/tn-verification-gate.md`, `agents/feature-verifier.md` | Consumers/describers of `acceptance-criteria-structured` | Confirmed; feature-verifier.md reference is descriptive only (line 33), not a second enforcement point |\\n| 16 | `docs/workflow-layers/*.json`, `docs/workflow-result.json`, `docs/dh-workflow-graph.json`, `graphify-out/*` | Generated/historical snapshots referencing T0/TN | Confirmed generated (see \\\"Last generated\\\" timestamps / `snapshot_status: historical-generated-output`) \u2014 NOT hand-edit targets; if swarm-task-planner.md's structure changes, run `dh:meta-workflow-graph-refresh` afterward, do not edit these files directly |\\n\\n## Code-Producers\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/dependencies.py` \u2014 `BookendValidator` class (lines ~276-391) implements all 5 structural rules correctly, including the exact rule this bug violates (`acceptance_criteria_structured` non-empty \u21d2 both T0 and TN required). **It is dead code at runtime** \u2014 imported and exported (`sam_schema/__init__.py:30,71`) and exercised only by its own unit tests.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/dh_core/operations.py` \u2014 `create_plan` (line 202), `append_task` (line 621), `finalize_plan` (line 668). These are the unified CLI+MCP operation layer and the only place a validator call could be inserted once. None currently reference `Bookend` anything; only generic `Model.model_validate` (field-level, not structural) runs.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/sam_plan.py` \u2014 Typer CLI `create`/`finalize`/`validate` commands (lines 286, 458-540) route through the same `operations.py` functions \u2014 a fix in `operations.py` covers both CLI and MCP surfaces without touching this file.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 MCP `sam_plan` action dispatch (`_sam_plan_create` line 214, `_sam_plan_finalize` line 352-370) \u2014 thin wrappers over `operations.py`, same conclusion.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/{local_yaml.py:716, github_task.py:560, beads.py:972}` \u2014 each backend's `finalize_plan` only flips state; no structural check. A fix belongs above this layer (in `operations.py`), not duplicated three times per backend.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` \u2014 the LLM-instruction-only enforcement (Bookend Task Generation + self-check step 12) is the *sole* current enforcement mechanism, and it is advisory (agent-followed), not machine-checked.\\n\\n## Code-Consumers\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/t0-baseline-capture.md` \u2014 reads `acceptance-criteria-structured` from the plan; assumes it is being invoked at all (i.e., assumes a T0 task exists to dispatch it).\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/tn-verification-gate.md` \u2014 same assumption for TN; produces the `TN-verification` artifact that `complete-implementation` reads.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` (lines 300-324) \u2014 Pre-Phase-1 TN Verification Check treats an absent `TN-verification` artifact as \\\"no structured criteria, proceed\\\" (mermaid label line 318: `\\\"No structured criteria \u2014 proceed to Phase 1\\\"`). This label is factually wrong when criteria exist but bookends were never generated \u2014 it silently masks exactly the failure mode #3277 describes. This is the concrete downstream harm.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 \\\"Bookend Task Ordering\\\" section documents dispatch-ordering guarantees (T0 first, TN last) that don't hold if bookends were never created; nothing in the dispatch loop notices their absence (confirmed no bookend logic in `sam_schema/dispatch.py` or `core/quality_gates.py`).\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-verifier.md` (line 33) \u2014 descriptive reference to `tn-verification-gate` re-running `acceptance-criteria-structured` checks; not a second gate, just documentation of intent.\\n\\n## Code-Other-References\\n\\n- `sam_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 `Task.is_bookend` / `Task.bookend_type` fields (lines 220-224), `BookendType` enum (line 105), `Plan.acceptance_criteria_structured` (line 298). Schema source of truth; unaffected by a fix but must stay in sync with any validator wiring change.\\n- `sam_schema/core/task_backend_types.py`, `sam_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py`, `sam_schema/readers/{manifest_reader,normalize,frontmatter_reader,yaml_reader}.py`, `sam_schema/core/backends/{memory,content,gist_task_layer}.py`, `sam_schema/cli_inputs.py` \u2014 all touch `bookend`/`is-bookend`/`acceptance-criteria-structured` field plumbing (serialize/deserialize/normalize) but contain no structural enforcement logic; grep-confirmed, no behavior change expected from a fix scoped to enforcement wiring.\\n- `sam_schema/dispatch.py`, `sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py` \u2014 grep-confirmed to contain **no** bookend-specific logic, consistent with `docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md`'s claim that \\\"No special handling is needed in the dispatch loop\\\" (T0/TN dispatch via ordinary priority/dependency ordering).\\n\\n## Documentation\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` \u2014 P4_BOOKEND flow (lines 395-421) and TN-artifact consumption (lines 533-547, 565-567) document the intended contract accurately but describe it as a given, with no mention that enforcement is currently instruction-only.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` \u2014 `is-bookend`/`bookend-type` field docs (lines 292-293, 388-389); accurate, no change needed for a validator-wiring fix.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/README.md`, `plugins/development-harness/AGENTS.md` \u2014 user-facing T0/TN descriptions; accurate at a high level, no change needed.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/*.json`, `docs/workflow-result.json`, `docs/dh-workflow-graph.json`, `graphify-out/*` \u2014 generated snapshots (confirmed via \\\"Last generated\\\" / `snapshot_status: historical-generated-output` markers). **Do not hand-edit.** If the fix restructures `swarm-task-planner.md`'s Bookend Task Generation section or self-check, run `dh:meta-workflow-graph-refresh` afterward per that skill's own trigger condition.\\n\\n## Configuration/CI\\n\\n- `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml` (line 244, `uv run -q --locked pytest`) \u2014 already runs `tests_sam/test_dependencies.py`'s full `BookendValidator` unit suite; these pass today and will continue to pass regardless of whether the validator is ever wired in, so CI green is not evidence the underlying defect is fixed. No existing CI job asserts end-to-end that a `finalize`/`create` call is rejected when structured criteria exist without bookends \u2014 that is a coverage gap this item's fix should close (new test in `tests_sam/` exercising `operations.create_plan`/`finalize_plan`, not just the validator class directly).\\n- No other workflow (`auto-rebase.yml`, `backlog-sync.yml`, `bump-marketplace.yml`, `claude-code-review.yml`, `claude.yml`, `copilot-setup-steps.yml`, `main-ci-health-check.yml`, `quality-gate-audit.yml`) references `sam_schema`, `tests_sam`, or `swarm-task-planner` \u2014 grep-confirmed, none affected.\\n\\n## Agent Instructions\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` \u2014 Bookend Task Generation (\u00a7328-391) and self-check step 12 (\u00a7605-612) are the only current enforcement mechanism and are advisory/LLM-followed, not machine-checked. This is the root-cause candidate for \\\"instruction-following failure\\\" \u2014 but the presence of an unwired, fully-correct `BookendValidator` (finding #5-9 above) means the more durable fix is schema-level enforcement, not a stronger prompt. Both should be considered candidate fixes; classification agent should weigh instruction-strengthening vs. schema-gap-closing as the primary vs. defense-in-depth remedy.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/t0-baseline-capture.md`, `agents/tn-verification-gate.md` \u2014 consumers, no changes needed for a validator-wiring fix; cross-listed above.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-verifier.md` \u2014 descriptive-only reference, no changes needed.\\n\\n## Ecosystem Completeness Checklist (5-question pass on the material systems)\\n\\n**`BookendValidator` (dependencies.py) + its absent call sites (operations.py/server.py/backends):**\\n1. What breaks if this changes (validator gets wired in)? \u2014 Plans with structured criteria and no T0/TN will start failing `create`/`finalize`/`append_task` where they previously silently succeeded. This is the intended fix but is a **breaking change for any in-flight drafting-state plan** that already lacks bookends (including `Pb31107bf` itself, if still in drafting/ready state) \u2014 needs a migration/backfill note, not just a code change.\\n2. Who/what consumes this? \u2014 CLI (`sam_plan.py`), MCP (`server.py`), all three backends transitively; ultimately `implement-feature`/`complete-implementation` skills and the T0/TN agents.\\n3. Is there a test guarding it? \u2014 Yes at the unit level (`test_dependencies.py`), **no** at the integration level (`operations.py` call path) \u2014 this is the gap to close.\\n4. Does documentation reference it accurately? \u2014 `backlog-item-lifecycle.md` and `TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` describe the intended contract but not that enforcement is currently absent; no doc change strictly required by a wiring fix, but the lifecycle doc could note the new hard-fail behavior post-fix.\\n5. Backward-compat/migration concern? \u2014 Yes (see #1): existing plans/backlog items with structured criteria and missing bookends will need either a migration script (see `plugins/development-harness/scripts/migrate_plan_artifacts.py` as a precedent pattern) or a one-time audit before the validator is made hard-enforcing.\\n\\n**`complete-implementation` TN Verification Check mermaid (SKILL.md:317-318):**\\n1. What breaks if this changes? \u2014 Correcting the \\\"artifact absent \u21d2 no structured criteria\\\" label to distinguish \\\"no structured criteria\\\" from \\\"criteria exist but bookends missing\\\" changes orchestrator behavior from silent-proceed to a warn-or-block path for the latter case.\\n2. Who/what consumes this? \u2014 The orchestrator running `/dh:complete-implementation`.\\n3. Is there a test guarding it? \u2014 No automated test found for this SKILL.md's mermaid/procedure text (it's prose/diagram, not code) \u2014 verification is manual/agent-followed only.\\n4. Does documentation reference it accurately? \u2014 This IS the documentation; it is the artifact that needs correcting.\\n5. Backward-compat concern? \u2014 Low \u2014 tightening this check only adds a new warn/block branch; does not remove existing behavior for the already-passing case.\\n\\nSTATUS: DONE \u2014 Impact Radius written (16-row systems inventory, 6 categories, scope expansion flagged: BookendValidator exists but is never called from any plan create/finalize path \u2014 schema-level gap, not just an agent instruction-following miss).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 development-harness /dh:work-backlog-item work --auto #3268, plan Pb31107bf\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-28\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Root-Cause Analysis\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T15:15:33.805649Z</sub>\\n\\n## 5-Whys Chain\\n\\n**CLAIM 1: Plan Pb31107bf with non-empty `acceptance-criteria-structured` has zero bookend tasks**\\n- EVIDENCE: Direct plan read via SAM MCP tool \u2014 plan shows 6 `acceptance-criteria-structured` entries and task list [T1\u2013T6] with no T0 or TN tasks\\n- VERIFIED: yes\\n\\n**CLAIM 2: swarm-task-planner has a documented mandatory self-check at Phase 4 Step 12 that should validate bookend presence**\\n- EVIDENCE: Read \u2014 `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` lines 605-612: \\\"Bookend presence check (when `acceptance-criteria-structured` is non-empty)\\\" mandates exactly one T0, one TN, proper dependencies; failure blocks registration\\n- VERIFIED: yes\\n\\n**CLAIM 3: A `BookendValidator` class exists in sam_schema with full unit test coverage and encodes all bookend validation rules**\\n- EVIDENCE: Read \u2014 `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/dependencies.py` lines 276-391 define `BookendValidator` class with methods to query T0, TN, implementation tasks, and validate dependency chains\\n- VERIFIED: yes\\n\\n**CLAIM 4: BookendValidator is exported from sam_schema package but never called from any plan write path**\\n- EVIDENCE: Bash \u2014 `grep -r \\\"BookendValidator\\\" --include=\\\"*.py\\\" plugins/development-harness/ | grep -v test_` returns only: `__init__.py` (export), `core/dependencies.py` (definition). Zero calls from `create_plan`, `finalize_plan`, or `append_task` in `dh_core/operations.py` or backends.\\n- VERIFIED: yes\\n- DEPENDS ON: Claim 3\\n\\n**CLAIM 5: The agent's Phase 4 Step 12 self-check is either never executed or the check logic itself is incomplete, because no validation gate exists in the control flow**\\n- EVIDENCE: The control flow from plan creation \u2192 plan finalization follows `dh_core/operations.py:create_plan()` \u2192 backend write \u2192 no `BookendValidator` instantiation or call anywhere in the path. The agent's documented self-check instruction (CLAIM 2) cannot execute a schema validation that exists outside the agent's scope.\\n- VERIFIED: yes\\n- DEPENDS ON: Claims 1, 2, 4\\n\\n## Root Cause\\n\\n**Code/Schema Gap**: A `BookendValidator` exists with complete logic and full unit test coverage, but is structurally isolated from the plan-write operations (`create_plan`, `finalize_plan`, `append_task`). The validator is never instantiated or called from any backend or MCP handler. Therefore, even a correctly-behaving swarm-task-planner agent cannot trigger the validation \u2014 it has no effect on runtime behavior.\\n\\nThe immediate cause of plan Pb31107bf's missing bookends is that no schema validation layer enforced the bookend-presence rule at plan-registration time. The root cause is the design gap between where validation logic lives (isolated validator class) and where it needs to execute (in the write paths).\\n\\n**Why the gap exists**: The validator was implemented (sam_schema/core/dependencies.py) and tested, but the integration \u2014 calling it from `create_plan`, `finalize_plan`, or `append_task` \u2014 was never completed. This is traceable to a missing wire-up task between the validator's completion and the write-path integration, not to agent behavior or documentation issues.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"85a5749501c1de1ae425ba0afac9076ae72359cfdf56be26002cfd720d1f4360\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRRs4Tw\"}"}